(r"""**ST6 — FUNDING IS A DERIVED BAND, NEVER A COIN STORE.** [REFINED 2026-10-18 (fp-final) — the brief's "the ONE upkeep-shaped sink (the `UPKEEP_LEDGERS` row the champions volume uses)" does not exist: `UPKEEP_LEDGERS = ['deployments']`, `advanceTreasury(settlement, options = {})` takes no worldState and is called once from the frozen kernel, and CH-r1-5 struck CH's row for that reason.] A holder's funding band is derived each read from what it has: a settlement from its prosperity rung (`prosperityRank01`), a creed from its standing in the holder's seat town, a person from its purse band (CH's derived purse), an UNTIED holder from nothing (its sites only wear). The DM may set the band by hand (it then holds until the DM clears it). Coin upkeep joins W-SEAT SEAT-8's `UPKEEP_LEDGERS` widening car as a fourth member beside `civilContests`, `interventions` and CH's retainers — the SLOT; when it lands the band reads the paid share.""",
r"""**ST6 — FUNDING IS A DERIVED BAND, NEVER A COIN STORE; THE DM'S BAND IS A CEILING.** [REFINED 2026-10-18 (fp-final) — the brief's "the ONE upkeep-shaped sink (the `UPKEEP_LEDGERS` row the champions volume uses)" does not exist: `UPKEEP_LEDGERS = ['deployments']`, `advanceTreasury(settlement, options = {})` takes no worldState and is called once from the frozen kernel.] A holder's DERIVED band is read each tick from what it has: a settlement from its prosperity label (`settlementFundingBand`, §2.4 — THE ONE settlement band, which THE PATROLS' pay gate reads too), a creed from its standing in the holder's seat town, a person from its purse band (CH's derived purse), an UNTIED holder from nothing (its sites only wear). The DM may set a band by hand (`fundingSet`), and it is a CEILING: the EFFECTIVE band is `min(fundingSet, derived)` on the order `unfunded < meagre < funded < lavish`, so a holder whose prosperity falls lets its sites go even under a DM's band — the owner's "these areas can also simply be abandonded due to lower prosperity" fires on every world now, before any treasury lights — and the DM's band can only hold a site LOWER than the holder's means (a lord who stops paying). To keep a poor town's keep manned regardless, the DM re-garrisons it by `SITE_HOLDER` (author): the DM's hand is total through the record, never through a band that outbids the world. COIN is the W-COIN slot (RULINGS-ROUND2 D): ONE upkeep law (`treasury.js :: computeUpkeep`, "ONE LAW PARAMETERIZED BY LEDGER"), widened by `UPKEEP_LEDGERS` members each with its caller in the same act — W-SEAT SEAT-8's `civilContests` · `interventions` (their charters) and FP's `sites` · `retainers` (CH) · `patrols` (PR): one roster, one law. FP's three ride ONE leaf-first car, because the frozen kernel's only call passes no worldState ("`advanceTreasury(sieged, { interval: tickInterval, tick: worldState.tick, deployment, blockade, rules: simulationRules })`"): the holder's roll is carried on the settlement record `advanceTreasury` already receives, written by the owning stage through its `settlementUpdates` and read the next tick (CH OD-CH-10's car; PLAUSIBLE, measured at that unit) — never a leaf inside `treasury.js` reading worldState, never a kernel line. When it lands, the derived band reads the PAID share. """ + C + r"""ST-r2-1 (RULINGS-ROUND2b: the DM's band a ceiling over the prosperity-derived band; the rows the W-COIN slot with a named car) · SEAMS-r2-12 (COIN separated from the BAND; the settlement-keyed band exported for the owner's patrol word "also size and number of patrols gated by tier, population, and prosperity and internal secruity").]"""),
